# Brain / AYAS durable runtime state — regenerated by the app, never hand-authored.
# data/brain/README.md stays tracked; these subtrees are local working state.
/data/brain/queue/
/data/brain/autonomy/
/data/brain/ayas-intents/
/data/brain/experience/
/data/brain/execution/
/data/brain/selfheal/
/data/brain/memory/
/data/brain/phone-access/
# Package C's isolated self-improvement execution root (M15) — only the
# execution/ subtree (gate/gate-log/journal/authority-lock), narrower than
# the parent so it can later legitimately hold tracked documentation or
# schema material. Untracked evidence under here made the repo look dirty
# to AyasExecutionRevalidation's own cleanliness check, aborting every real
# execution before any mutation — this rule fixes that without touching
# Package C's revalidation semantics themselves.
/data/brain/self-improvement/execution/

# M17 — frozen, immutable AI-generated patch artifacts (AyasPatchArtifact).
# Durable runtime evidence, same status as the execution/ subtree above: never
# hand-authored, regenerated by the app. Sandbox drafting itself happens
# entirely outside this repo (an os.tmpdir() git worktree, destroyed after use
# — see AyasPatchSandbox.ts) and never touches this directory or the real
# working tree until a patch is frozen here.
/data/brain/self-improvement/patch-artifacts/

# M18 — durable MICRO_SAFE micro-item evidence (AyasMicroItem). Same status
# as patch-artifacts/ above: regenerated by the app, never hand-authored.
# The persistent batch integration worktree itself lives entirely outside
# this repo (a fixed os.tmpdir() path — see AyasMicroBatchWorktree.ts) and
# never touches this directory or the real working tree until a batch is
# actually executed through Package C.
/data/brain/self-improvement/micro-items/

# M19 — durable per-item Graphify PASS/FAIL evidence (AyasGraphifyEvidenceStore).
# Same status as patch-artifacts/ and micro-items/ above: regenerated by the
# app, never hand-authored. Without this rule, the first real per-item
# Graphify-evidenced execution would leave this new subtree untracked, which
# would make AYAS's own repoClean/revalidation checks see a dirty tree and
# refuse further discovery/execution — a self-inflicted deadlock.
/data/brain/self-improvement/graphify-evidence/

# M22 — durable goal state (AyasGoalStore) and external capability research
# findings (AyasExternalResearchStore). Same status as the sibling
# self-improvement subtrees above: regenerated by the app, never
# hand-authored, and must stay untracked so AYAS's own repoClean check
# never trips on its own durable state.
/data/brain/self-improvement/goals/
/data/brain/self-improvement/external-research/

# M21.4 — durable sandbox-unvalidatable suppression records
# (AyasSandboxUnvalidatableStore). Same status as the sibling
# self-improvement subtrees above: regenerated by the app, never
# hand-authored, and must stay untracked so AYAS's own repoClean check
# never trips on its own durable state.
/data/brain/self-improvement/sandbox-unvalidatable/

# AYAS CONTINUOUS EXTERNAL INTELLIGENCE sprint — durable research-scheduler
# state (AyasResearchSchedulerStateStore) and per-source LIGHT-scan check
# state (AyasResearchSourceStateStore). Same status as the sibling
# self-improvement subtrees above: regenerated by the app, never
# hand-authored, and must stay untracked so AYAS's own repoClean check never
# trips on its own durable state.
/data/brain/self-improvement/research/
/data/brain/self-improvement/research-sources/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C.2B.12 (Sprint 199) — data/projects is external-runtime authority data.
#
# Runtime storage authority is the ATOLYE_RUNTIME_ROOT + the authority control
# plane (RuntimeAuthorityTransition / *Rollback / the generation marker), NOT
# git. Every file under data/projects — the milestone snapshots included — is
# regenerated / owned by the running app, so git stops tracking it. The files
# stay on disk: `git rm -r --cached data/projects` removed them from the index
# only, it never deleted a worktree file.
#
# This is the narrowest rule that does it — data/brain (README.md stays
# tracked), data/e2e-output and every other data/ subtree are unaffected.
# To deliberately pin a specific snapshot back into git: `git add -f <path>`.
/data/projects/

# PipelineJobMutationLock's process-local mutex dir — anywhere it appears.
**/.pipeline-jobs.lock/
/.venv-wake/
/bin/whisper/

# onnxruntime-web WASM (copied from node_modules by scripts/setup-wake-assets.ts)
/public/ort/

# wrangler build cache / local state (cloudflare/ayas-phone-gateway) — per-machine, not committed
.wrangler/
